{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised","id":1417075,"title":"Sorcerer Revised","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-06T16:16:11-07:00","id":1417075,"title":"Sorcerer Revised","content":"Hello mage fans, so I have a question about Sorcerer Revised. I am not entirely sure I understand the path rating, dice pool, and success system for the rules. I tried googling things, no real luck, and I tried searching around here, and also no real luck. I did happen to find the Sorcerer's Companion fan product on DriveThru which I bought and love (too bad there are no pod versions) and while it made me want to play it, it didn't help me so much understand it. <br /> <br /> For the record I would plan on using it with the 20th Anniversary Edition of Mage, though I also own the Mage Revised core. I also own the WOD Sorcerer Hege wizard book, in addition to me owning Sorcerer Revised. (Not sure which is more 'accurate' as far as 2020 rules are concerned but yeah). <br /> <br /> So yeah, any help on how the successes would be divided would be much appreciated. <br /> <br /> PS. I am not sure if this is a general WOD question or a Mage Ascension question, but as Sorcerer Revised is technically a Mage book I am putting this here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T00:11:14-07:00","id":1417111,"title":"","content":"If you are the storyteller and your players don't mind you make your on interpretation of the limits of the paths, then I suggest you read Sorcerer older edition. The rules are much more simplified (which works for me) and also the writting and explanation of what is magic are more charming than revised IMO. Also I personally enjoy the artwork more. Old Sorcerer is a great book. I find that the revised edition tried to make path magic too detailed and complex.<br /> <br /> edit: The big loss, of course, are psychic numina, which are not in the older book. But to be fair, they do look more simple than the updated paths so you might still be able to use it together with the old book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","user":"Rucun","date":". 10-07-2020, 03:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T08:48:52-07:00","id":1417149,"title":"","content":"In old WOD sorcerer, the effects are similar to vampire thaumaturgy in that each dot gives you greater power a path and the difficulty is based on the level of power you're trying to invoke. In this system, number of successes just determines how well you perform the effect and a single success is good enough for most things outside of combat. Problems arise in that sorcerers are the only splat that require multiple turns to invoke any effect beyond first level. The logical result of that is players forced to sit around doing nothing for up to six turns while their character does nothing but cast a single spell and still get pasted by anything in WOD, including a vanilla human with a gun.<br /> <br /> Revised sorcerer is broken and not in the OP way. Effects are split between multiple aspects that you have to split successes between and the amount of successes you can spend on each aspect is determined before the roll by declaring what dot level you are casting at. Unfortunately, the dot level also determines the difficulty of the casting despite the fact that larger effects require More successes and casting take as many turns as the dot level you use.<br /> <br /> This means casting hellfire as a 5 dot effect(10 dice) will end with the character taking 5 turns to cast a spell that does 2 dice of lethal damage to 1 target in touch range and maybe 1 extra success to improve one aspect. On the other hand, that same mage casting hellfire as a 3 dot effect will take 3 turns to get 2-3 extra successes that you can spend to enhance that, but casting at hellfire 1 leaves the sorcerer with 6 successes it can't use. The only way around the difficulty is to spend mana, which is a very limited resource unless you spend 2 of you 5 starting dots in mana manipulation, and the time constraints can only be worked around by &quot;hanging&quot; spells(casting them before-hand, but waiting to complete them), but you can only &quot;hang&quot; up to your willpower in spells.<br /> <br /> This isn't playable without ST houserules. My recommendation is to throw out the multi-turn rule completely, select one of the Aspects as something the character automatically gets when they cast at higher dot levels and un-cap the amount of successes a player can spend on other aspects. This way the hellfire sorcerer can cast at dot 5 and get 10 dice of damage even on one success or cast at dot 1 and spend those extra successes to effect multiple target farther away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T09:28:33-07:00","id":1417157,"title":"","content":"Okay so I was mentally right. I wasn't missing something in how I thought I read it. I did read it right, and what I read made no sense. <br /> <br /> To cast a third dot power with 3 levels in one aspect and two levels in another aspect would need 3 success and three turns. To cast a five dot power that has say 5 in one aspect and 5 in another aspect and maybe 5 in a third aspect would be 12 successes with a difficulty of 9. <br /> <br /> Okay, screw that. <br /> <br /> So yeah, the aspect system goes. What you can do is based on the dots you have in a path. <br /> <br /> If you have Conjuration 3 then you can cast an effect of 3 or fewer dots. Meaning you could control three largish objects from over 100 feet away with some fine control. <br /> <br /> So looking at things the various changes I would make are: <br /> <br /> 1 success is needed to activate. <br /> Difficulty is dot + 3. <br /> Casting takes 1 turn no matter the dot rating. <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> So basically the end result is use the basic ideas from say World of Darkness Sorcerer the Hedge Wizards Handbook and the psychic stuff form Sorcerer Revised and then make some changes to balance things out a bit. <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> I thank you both for the information though I have to admit I am kind of disappointed in the fact that the book basically fails. Too bad there isn't Sorcerer: The 20th Anniversary Edition because that would be brilliant. <br /> <br /> I love mage but its complex magic requires a particular mindset that while I have sometimes I don't always have (or want to activate) and so I was liking the idea of these Paths. Probably because I really like Vampire Thaumaturgy and looked at the Sorcerer Paths as a sort of mortal version of that. <br /> <br /> So yeah, thanks all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T22:58:24-07:00","id":1417264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1417157#post1417157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay so I was mentally right. I wasn't missing something in how I thought I read it. I did read it right, and what I read made no sense.<br /> <br /> To cast a third dot power with 3 levels in one aspect and two levels in another aspect would need 3 success and three turns. To cast a five dot power that has say 5 in one aspect and 5 in another aspect and maybe 5 in a third aspect would be 12 successes with a difficulty of 9.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, To get 3 levels in one aspect and 2 in another would require 4 successes total. The first success counts for every aspect, but all successes afterwards must be counted individually. So to get 5 in 3 aspects would require 13( 1 for the first success and 12 more to add +4 to each aspect)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1417157#post1417157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you have Conjuration 3 then you can cast an effect of 3 or fewer dots. Meaning you could control three largish objects from over 100 feet away with some fine control.<br /> <br /> So looking at things the various changes I would make are:<br /> <br /> 1 success is needed to activate.<br /> Difficulty is dot + 3.<br /> Casting takes 1 turn no matter the dot rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might also be good to note that the aspects in Sorcerer Revised are more powerful in many areas than the straight paths in WOD sorcerer. For example: Conjuration 6 is required to move 3 objects of up to human size, but in Revised 3 success does that and 6 successes let's you move 100 related objects or 25 un-related with size as a different aspect. The Biggest problem with Revised(besides the dumb turn rules) is that Getting those successes is impossible.<br /> <br /> My take is merging both WOD and Revised editions of Sorcerer. If you instead have the dot rating be the power &quot;aspect&quot; of the spell(damage dice for hellfire, object size for conjuration, number of people for conveyance, time period for divination, etc, etc) then it'll means 1 less aspect to split dice for and also make more sense as to why the spell is more difficult(because you're doing something hard). I reccomend keeping aspects because scoring more than 1 success in WOD sorcerer rules is meaningless.<br /> <br /> I'd also reccomend changing the dice pool for paths to Attribute + Path rating and for psychic powers to rolling Permanent Willpower. It makes both practices feel different, gives you more dice to work with, and makes using sorcery or psychic powers cheaper on XP(which it should be, these aren't as strong as other supernatural powers so making them cost the same as mage spheres and out-of-clan disciplines is insane).<br /> <br /> Finally I say remove the &quot;no multi-path rituals&quot; rule. I personally enjoy ruling that enchanting/alchemy let's you craft artifacts/potions with an effect from another path you know at equal or lower rating to your enchanting/alchemy. I also like ruling that Mana manipulation let's you change the obscure resource/curse requirement on enchanted/alchemical objects to a mana-cost equal to enchantment level per scene/X number of turns(depending on effect).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T02:18:06-07:00","id":1417290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1417157#post1417157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay </div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerer Rev. is a Mage book, so they make it more Mage, especially on disadvantages. For example if you want to invoke a little bigger spells you must spend much time preparing it<br /> <br /> I also like Sorcerer, Mage is great and interesting but complex after all. Sorcerer, however, is much simpler and easier","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T08:26:28-07:00","id":1417323,"title":"","content":"<i>Sorcerer Revised </i>is incredibly versatile, and includes within its pages a number of suggestions for how to make hedge magicians more or less powerful than the baseline presented. They discuss everything for changing requisite casting times, to changing base difficulties, I think even the efficacy of individual successes. This is scattered throughout the book, but there at least two places in the book I know for a fact they go into tweaking mechanics to achieve whatever balance or flavor: one is in a box found in the section explaining the mechanics of casting (this section immediately precedes the laundry list of ritual paths/non-psychic stuff); the place they discuss it is towards the end of the book, amidst discussions of sorcerers' and hedge magicians' place in a WoD chronicle (I think the rules for making up new paths is around there too).<br /> <br /> I've definitely commented on these forums in the past, and to others, that with just a handful of tweaks suggested in that book itself, you can basically make hedge magic every bit the equal of vampiric blood magic, and frankly <i>moreso</i>, given the rules about &quot;hanging&quot; spells that basically put a vancian spin on the system, inasmuch as hanging a number of spells for later use is practically the same thing as preparing spells in D&amp;D.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T08:29:19-07:00","id":1417324,"title":"","content":"What do you guys think of the factions in Sorcerer Revised?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T08:38:05-07:00","id":1417325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1417324#post1417324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you guys think of the factions in Sorcerer Revised?</div> </div> </div> </div> Completely fascinating, zany fun. You basically get the blueprint for running an entire sorcerer chronicle just from this book, and they have sorcerers doing some world-saving-level stuff no less. I would definitely use this stuff if I were going to run a sorcerer game, and what's more, of all the &quot;lesser&quot;/third-tier supernaturals in the WoD (so, the folks who did not even get a hardcover book,) it really seems like sorcerers are the only ones that, out of the box/by the book, can have their own cool adventures that don't have to do with either being some main gameline supernatural's lackey, or hunting a main gameline supernatural.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T09:48:35-07:00","id":1417334,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1417264#post1417264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, To get 3 levels in one aspect and 2 in another would require 4 successes total. The first success counts for every aspect, but all successes afterwards must be counted individually. So to get 5 in 3 aspects would require 13( 1 for the first success and 12 more to add +4 to each aspect)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, okay. I see. I'm not liking what I see, like at all, but I now see. <br /> <br /> (So my issue was that I was ignoring the 'starter' successin such a way that I was rolling it into the other needed successes rather than adding it on top. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1417264#post1417264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might also be good to note that the aspects in Sorcerer Revised are more powerful in many areas than the straight paths in WOD sorcerer. For example: Conjuration 6 is required to move 3 objects of up to human size, but in Revised 3 success does that and 6 successes let's you move 100 related objects or 25 un-related with size as a different aspect. The Biggest problem with Revised(besides the dumb turn rules) is that Getting those successes is impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I just noticed this. I mean I read both books but I didn't focus on the numbers per dot and your right, Revised leads to more powerful sorcerers. I do like that aspect though, I think the changes in that make a bit more sense. <br /> <br /> One thing I definitely would do is remove the 1 dot Conveyance thing about 'maybe your close won't come' bs. Nah. If you have the power, and you don't like botch terribly, your close will naturally come with you. <br /> <br /> ----<br /> <br /> My take is merging both WOD and Revised editions of Sorcerer. If you instead have the dot rating be the power &quot;aspect&quot; of the spell(damage dice for hellfire, object size for conjuration, number of people for conveyance, time period for divination, etc, etc) then it'll means 1 less aspect to split dice for and also make more sense as to why the spell is more difficult(because you're doing something hard). I reccomend keeping aspects because scoring more than 1 success in WOD sorcerer rules is meaningless.<br /> <br /> I'd also reccomend changing the dice pool for paths to Attribute + Path rating and for psychic powers to rolling Permanent Willpower. It makes both practices feel different, gives you more dice to work with, and makes using sorcery or psychic powers cheaper on XP(which it should be, these aren't as strong as other supernatural powers so making them cost the same as mage spheres and out-of-clan disciplines is insane).<br /> <br /> Finally I say remove the &quot;no multi-path rituals&quot; rule. I personally enjoy ruling that enchanting/alchemy let's you craft artifacts/potions with an effect from another path you know at equal or lower rating to your enchanting/alchemy. I also like ruling that Mana manipulation let's you change the obscure resource/curse requirement on enchanted/alchemical objects to a mana-cost equal to enchantment level per scene/X number of turns(depending on effect).[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I like the idea that the base effect is 'free' based on your Path Rating. I am a Conveyance expert with 5 dots, which means 1 success grants me anywhere from 1 to 5 dots in the basic conveyance aspect, while other successes can boost the other aspects above the initial starting base level. <br /> <br /> I wonder if maybe having it so that dots above the base effect can give auto successes to other aspects. Example, I have 5 dots in Conveyance but I only want to implement the one dot level of the main conveyance aspect, this gives me four dots I can use as successes to boost that one dot effect a bit higher. <br /> <br /> On Attribute + Path, yeah, I can see the great benefits of that. It means basically that as your capability in the path increases so does your knowledge of what the Path does. <br /> <br /> (The amusing thing about making this potentially Willpower roll based is my arguing in the Vampire thread about how I dislike Thaumaturgy being Willpower rather than Attribute + Ability, hehe). <br /> <br /> Oh yeah, I agree. There is absolutely no reason that a sorcerer shouldn't be allowed to combine effects when they know things. Especially the whole alchemy and enchanting path, which cries out for being combined. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1417290#post1417290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorcerer Rev. is a Mage book, so they make it more Mage, especially on disadvantages. For example if you want to invoke a little bigger spells you must spend much time preparing it<br /> <br /> I also like Sorcerer, Mage is great and interesting but complex after all. Sorcerer, however, is much simpler and easier</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I get that. I don't like it as if you own Mage then you probably will focus on Mage rules while the whole point of Sorcerer is NOT to be a mage. Is NOT to have crazy (awesome but crazy) vast sphere magic. So yeah, making it Mage just seems out of touch to me. <br /> <br /> But this was 20 years ago (wow by the way) so shrug. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So yeah, like you said, Sorcerer is simpler and easier to both understand and use. And honestly sometimes one wants to have mighty powers but not also have to do vast maths. <br /> <br /> --------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1417323#post1417323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Sorcerer Revised </i>is incredibly versatile, and includes within its pages a number of suggestions for how to make hedge magicians more or less powerful than the baseline presented. They discuss everything for changing requisite casting times, to changing base difficulties, I think even the efficacy of individual successes. This is scattered throughout the book, but there at least two places in the book I know for a fact they go into tweaking mechanics to achieve whatever balance or flavor: one is in a box found in the section explaining the mechanics of casting (this section immediately precedes the laundry list of ritual paths/non-psychic stuff); the place they discuss it is towards the end of the book, amidst discussions of sorcerers' and hedge magicians' place in a WoD chronicle (I think the rules for making up new paths is around there too).<br /> <br /> I've definitely commented on these forums in the past, and to others, that with just a handful of tweaks suggested in that book itself, you can basically make hedge magic every bit the equal of vampiric blood magic, and frankly <i>moreso</i>, given the rules about &quot;hanging&quot; spells that basically put a vancian spin on the system, inasmuch as hanging a number of spells for later use is practically the same thing as preparing spells in D&amp;D.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I love those modification side bars. The one about making Difficulty 3 + Path Level rather than 4 is great. As is the one about reducing Time so casting is easier. Also interesting is the Willpower change. <br /> <br /> Buuut, the one thing they don't suggest, is how to make Successes more logical. <br /> <br /> The book also lacks examples of characters rolling their powers and such in ways that clear up all issues. <br /> <br /> That all said, yeah, your right, it does understand that some people might want slightly different systems, and that is really cool about it. <br /> <br /> I like Mage, I really do, but sometimes I want something more Discipline and Thaumaturgy like when it comes to playing - minus the whole being a Vampire thing. Which is why I was like &quot;ooh Sorcerer, that will cover what I want.&quot; But it doesn't really. At least not as written. Not entirely anyway. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T18:56:29-07:00","id":1417408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1417325#post1417325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Completely fascinating, zany fun. You basically get the blueprint for running an entire sorcerer chronicle just from this book, and they have sorcerers doing some world-saving-level stuff no less. I would definitely use this stuff if I were going to run a sorcerer game, and what's more, of all the &amp;quot;lesser&amp;quot;/third-tier supernaturals in the WoD (so, the folks who did not even get a hardcover book,) it really seems like sorcerers are the only ones that, out of the box/by the book, can have their own cool adventures that don't have to do with either being some main gameline supernatural's lackey, or hunting a main gameline supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cool! Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T23:21:32-07:00","id":1417418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1417334#post1417334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI like Mage, I really do, but sometimes I want something more Discipline and Thaumaturgy like when it comes to playing - minus the whole being a Vampire thing. Which is why I was like &quot;ooh Sorcerer, that will cover what I want.&quot; But it doesn't really. At least not as written. Not entirely anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you familiar with V20 Hunters Hunted II? They have Hedge Magic rules in there, though they only present three Paths (Curses, Divination, and Healing). You might want to run a comparison between that and WoD:Sorcerer to get a sense of what, if anything, changes in the 20th Anniversary version of Path Magic. Then use that information to decide how other Paths might be adapted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T09:00:14-07:00","id":1417459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1417418#post1417418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you familiar with V20 Hunters Hunted II? They have Hedge Magic rules in there, though they only present three Paths (Curses, Divination, and Healing). You might want to run a comparison between that and WoD:Sorcerer to get a sense of what, if anything, changes in the 20th Anniversary version of Path Magic. Then use that information to decide how other Paths might be adapted.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I was able to look into it and yeah, the way they did Healing for example is basically spot on how I would have wanted them to do it. hehe <br /> <br /> Sorcerer Revised Healing is a mess of random charts and confusing options whike WOD Sorcerer Healing is nice but lower powered then what I would have wanted. But V20 Hunters Hunted II took the ideas from WOD Sorcerer and boosted it up a little bit. So yeah, that adaptation to the 20th anniversary was great. <br /> <br /> Well mostly, I am not a fan of the whole sympathetic pain that one feels by healing another. <br /> <br /> I do find it sad that they took the Curses path, which had been made into Fortune, and then turned it back to Curses as I liked it giving both the good and the bad. <br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for the info, it was something useful to look up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T09:09:04-07:00","id":1417461,"title":"","content":"Charles Siegel one of the most prolific of the Vault Authors is working on Sorcerer 20, which I am glad because we need it! It was originally supposed to be out by now so I am guessing it\u2019s close to done. But you recommend the Sorcerers companion? I\u2019ll check it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T09:11:58-07:00","id":1417463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1417461#post1417461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charles Siegel one of the most prolific of the Vault Authors is working on Sorcerer 20, which I am glad because we need it! It was originally supposed to be out by now so I am guessing it\u2019s close to done. But you recommend the Sorcerers companion? I\u2019ll check it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerer's Companion doesn't houserule or fix any of the success issues that Sorcerer Revised had in it but it does have a lot of really cool rituals and such things. Plus it has a few paths that are fully path based and not aspect based which can be quickly used. <br /> <br /> That said, didn't know about Charles Siegel and his attempt on Sorcerer 20. Is he using WOD Sorcerer and Sorcerer Revised as his base or is he doing something completely new? <br /> <br /> Honestly, I hope its using the Paths as a basis from the previous books rather than making his own new system, but then, who knows, said new system could be awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T09:25:34-07:00","id":1417467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1417463#post1417463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorcerer's Companion doesn't houserule or fix any of the success issues that Sorcerer Revised had in it but it does have a lot of really cool rituals and such things. Plus it has a few paths that are fully path based and not aspect based which can be quickly used. <br /> <br /> That said, didn't know about Charles Siegel and his attempt on Sorcerer 20. Is he using WOD Sorcerer and Sorcerer Revised as his base or is he doing something completely new? <br /> <br /> Honestly, I hope its using the Paths as a basis from the previous books rather than making his own new system, but then, who knows, said new system could be awesome.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my understanding he will collect all the paths found in books, revise them for Mage 20, so I hope he gives rules for focuses and the like, and then add some of his own stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T14:41:42-07:00","id":1417484,"title":"","content":"I hope Charles Siegel does do the Sorcerer 20. I was very exited about running a Hedge Magicians game until I read this thread, and now I am frightened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T15:44:23-07:00","id":1417491,"title":"","content":"I wonder if you could just houserule M20 to give you a similar feel - low powered, gritty, very flavorful (e.g., real-world techniques).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T15:59:02-07:00","id":1417492,"title":"","content":"Well, as was mentioned elsewhere in this thread the rules do give a bunch of options on how to house rule things to make what one might want. <br /> <br /> Examples. <br /> <br /> Aspects. One option is to remove them in the sense that if you have Path 4 then you get access to 4 and below in all aspects for each roll. One success activates them all. Another option is that the main aspect is given free equal to Path dots while the other aspects are paid for by additional successes beyond the first dot being free. (So if you have Path 4 then the primary aspect is 4 with one success, but if you want another aspect at 2 dots then you need an additional success to pay for it). <br /> <br /> Personally, I went with the idea of rolling all features together into one general dot system. So if you have Path 4 then you can do anything from 4 downward. <br /> <br /> Willpower. You can increase or decrease the Willpower cost. Maybe add a Mana cost too. <br /> <br /> Personally, I like most powers being free but certain ones costing 1 Willpower. OR Mana, if you have that instead. This includes Alchemy, Conveyance, Enchanting plus some others. <br /> <br /> Difficulty. The official rule is Level + 4 for difficulty, but they also suggest making it Level + 3, putting it at par with say Thaumaturgy and such. <br /> <br /> I did that, made it Level + 3. <br /> <br /> Casting Time. Officially its level in turns but they suggest making it one turn. Which is what I did, all path castings are one turn, though some Rituals may be longer. Obviously Alchemy and Enchanting take longer too by their very nature. <br /> <br /> Basically, while there are elements that make one go &quot;huh???&quot; in general the path dots are interesting and could be easily kept writing wise as is. <br /> <br /> Oh, except for Healing, which is a bloody mess that makes no sense. So on Healing I recommend using either WOD Sorcerer or the Healing path in the V20 Hunters Hunted II book. (Which is what I am doing.) <br /> <br /> Just my thoughts of course. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T11:12:48-07:00","id":1417663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1417484#post1417484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope Charles Siegel does do the Sorcerer 20. I was very exited about running a Hedge Magicians game until I read this thread, and now I am frightened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't be frightened. Even with all the added complications it has, Sorcerer Revised is still simpler than Mage. It's just that there's been a trend to make it more and more complicated with each iteration (with Hunters Hunted II being a notable exception). <br /> <br /> If publishing Path write-ups that are compatible with HH2 is something that STV allows, I'd love to see it happen. I fear, though, that it would fall into the realm of \u201ctoo much duplicated material for Fair Use\u201d. Then again, the Enlightened Grimoire, Mystic Armoury, and Sources of Magic (also by Charles Siegel) are largely compendia of existing material, so there's that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T11:17:53-07:00","id":1417664,"title":"","content":"I chatted with Charles Siegel. He said his new product is waiting for an editor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T11:25:24-07:00","id":1417666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1417467#post1417467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From my understanding he will collect all the paths found in books, revise them for Mage 20, so I hope he gives rules for focuses and the like, and then add some of his own stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I like his work, I'm concerned that this may end up continuing the trend of increasingly overcomplicating Hedge Magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T11:29:35-07:00","id":1417667,"title":"","content":"Well, from buying his stuff so far he's very competent and responsible. My guess is it will be a more coherent version of Revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T11:39:32-07:00","id":1417670,"title":"","content":"Yeah; I also own all of his products, to the point that I'm willing to buy anything he writes sight unseen. That said, I'll feel more comfortable one I've bought it. <br /> <br /> What I'm hoping to see is something where the Tools and Aspects stuff are optional, so that if someone wants to use the Paths he's adapting for M20 as an expansion to the HH2 material, they can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T11:58:19-07:00","id":1417675,"title":"","content":"At the time I started work, the rules on the Vault were somewhat vague about whether standalone 20th anniversary books were allowed (things like the WoD20: Ghosthunters being kickstarted right now) so I had to lean in heavily on Mage, but also I wanted to put Extraordinary Citizens on equal footing to mystic sorcerers, so there's the complication of picking a Practice to determine tools and an Ability to add to a specified Attribute for rolls on the Path in my version (I'll say, it's been tested with a group including a 12 year old...game kept appropriate...so it's not overly complex as intended.)<br /> <br /> Sadly, I do need an editor, and am having trouble finding someone who can commit to it, so I don't have an ETA on it.<br /> <br /> Also, Dataweaver, Sources of Magic is not a compendium of existing material, it was created because there's no material giving depths to Nodes at any point in the Mage canon. Enlightened Grimoire and Mystic Armory very much are, though, and I won't run into any trouble with a sorcerer update as long as 1) it's in my words, not copy-pasted, 2) it's a rules update to 20th anniversary, not just a rewrite of Sorcerer Revised for Revised or the like (when I embark on projects like this, I ask the powers-that-be in advance to make sure it's kosher)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25057-janothar","name":"Janothar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T12:59:26-07:00","id":1417685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janothar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1417675#post1417675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the time I started work, the rules on the Vault were somewhat vague about whether standalone 20th anniversary books were allowed (things like the WoD20: Ghosthunters being kickstarted right now) so I had to lean in heavily on Mage, but also I wanted to put Extraordinary Citizens on equal footing to mystic sorcerers, so there's the complication of picking a Practice to determine tools and an Ability to add to a specified Attribute for rolls on the Path in my version (I'll say, it's been tested with a group including a 12 year old...game kept appropriate...so it's not overly complex as intended.)</div> </div> </div> </div> For what it's worth, my own preferred solution to the \u201cSleepers with magic\u201d issue is to expand on the way <b>Gods and Monsters</b> handled it: let Extraordinary Citizens and their mystic counterparts (defined as Sleepers who have a Focus) learn individual Rotes without the Sphere and Arete requirements, but with some sort of cost attached to using them (such as requiring a Willpower expenditure, or a higher XP cost to learn the Rote). I've tried several approaches to this, and the one I've been looking at recently involves building on your Rotes system in <b>Enlightened Grimoire</b>: add a Codified option costing N\u00d7(difference between the Rote's level and your ranking in its primary Sphere) that lets you learn and cast the Rote with insufficient Spheres and even Arete; and possibly add a system of cost reducers based on the Scars from the upcoming <b>Deviant</b> Chronicles of Darkness gameline. There would be a few additional restrictions if you're not Awakened, such as requiring the caster's Focus to use the same Practice and Instruments as the Rote. <br /> <br /> But as far as Paths go, I've advocated a Focus-based approach myself. I'm not opposed to it; I just think it should be presented as an <i>option</i> rather than a <i>mandate</i>. Likewise with the Aspects: first write the Path in a way that doesn't require Aspects, then follow that up with tweaks for those who like Aspects.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm open to serving as editor, of you'll have me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 10-11-2020, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T13:48:35-07:00","id":1417695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Janothar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1417675#post1417675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the time I started work, the rules on the Vault were somewhat vague about whether standalone 20th anniversary books were allowed (things like the WoD20: Ghosthunters being kickstarted right now) so I had to lean in heavily on Mage, but also I wanted to put Extraordinary Citizens on equal footing to mystic sorcerers, so there's the complication of picking a Practice to determine tools and an Ability to add to a specified Attribute for rolls on the Path in my version (I'll say, it's been tested with a group including a 12 year old...game kept appropriate...so it's not overly complex as intended.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly have an issue with the whole 'lets use the Mage paradigm to figure out out sorcerers work in the World of Darkness' because most uses of say Sorcerer or Hedge Magic or even psychic powers are for games without Mages being present. Its for when I am playing mortal magic users operating in the Word of Darkness, maybe as hunters (though I doubt as Hunters). Or maybe its for a Vampire game where I want something different. Or a werewolf game. But really mostly a mortal game where I would want characters with cool, fun, awesome supernatural abilities that doesn't involve the complexity of Sphere magic. <br /> <br /> So yeah to here that Mage specific elements are gonna be say front stage just worries me. <br /> <br /> Unless I am misinterpreting what you are saying, which could very much be true. <br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Also, it seems that modern 20th Anniversary Edition version of the World of Darkness has gone away from aspects, which to me is not just quite fine but something I approve of. <br /> --<br /> <br /> Speaking of Paths, I honestly have come to like Attribute + Path as the dice pool. I think having one's general knowledge of the path (based one the dots one has in it) as part of the dice pool makes more sense then regular, non-mystical knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T22:31:31-07:00","id":1418303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1417695#post1417695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it seems that modern 20th Anniversary Edition version of the World of Darkness has gone away from aspects, which to me is not just quite fine but something I approve of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weirdly enough WoD20 does have a splat with an aspect system. The Hsien in C20 use aspects like their earlier edition counterparts, but in a much different way.<br /> <br /> Hsien spend dice from their dicepool on aspects rather than rolled successes and a single success is all you need to cast an effect. In play this means casting bigger effects isn't gimped by success quotas while still making them risky to cast(you're more likely to botch with less dice after all). It's also A Lot faster since people don't need to roll as many dice or count their successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T13:30:26-07:00","id":1419079,"title":"","content":"Should note that Sorcerer Revised suffered greatly from the lack of an editor. There's tons, and I mean tons, of issues with that book between the sorcery and character creation rules. Things like the book saying that mana is a Latin word (it's not; it's Polynesian), having a 5pt Merit that's actually a flaw, and other things like the rules of sorcery literally changing each page (look at how weather control works, it references non-existent rules). The psychic powers were at least put together well.<br /> <br /> Would it be nice to have a working system for sorcery that actually is pretty flexible and fun? Yes<br /> Will we ever get that? Probably not from White Wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T21:37:49-07:00","id":1419119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1419079#post1419079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should note that Sorcerer Revised suffered greatly from the lack of an editor. There's tons, and I mean tons, of issues with that book between the sorcery and character creation rules. Things like the book saying that mana is a Latin word (it's not; it's Polynesian), having a 5pt Merit that's actually a flaw, and other things like the rules of sorcery literally changing each page (look at how weather control works, it references non-existent rules). The psychic powers were at least put together well.<br /> <br /> Would it be nice to have a working system for sorcery that actually is pretty flexible and fun? Yes<br /> Will we ever get that? Probably not from White Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually Polynesian Mana is a separate thing from the Latin Manna which was a hold over from Greek which was translating Hebrew Man, you know the old &quot;found Manna in the wilderness&quot;. Modern geeks seem to often conflate the two because they are esoteric concepts from two obscure metaphysical concepts.<br /> <br /> <br /> I feel we need some Kung Fu Numina, I'm working on it. The problem is a lot of the character build concepts would use things like Merits, but how CWOD merits work they are undesirable compared to NWOD/Exalted Merits.<br /> <br /> <br /> I want a Book Dedicated to Extraordinary Citizens and Enlightened Science in the hands of nonMages. And some Supernatural Martials Arts love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T21:39:47-07:00","id":1419120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1417664#post1417664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I chatted with Charles Siegel. He said his new product is waiting for an editor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh Beautiful!<br /> <br /> Say does anyone know when Drivethru is next going to do a half off sale on everything World of Darkness? I want to get a bunch of Vault books then. :P Isn't there a Halloween Sale like they used to do a decade ago?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T22:59:56-07:00","id":1419129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1417075-sorcerer-revised?p=1419119#post1419119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Actually Polynesian Mana is a separate thing from the Latin Manna which was a hold over from Greek which was translating Hebrew Man, you know the old &quot;found Manna in the wilderness&quot;. Modern geeks seem to often conflate the two because they are esoteric concepts from two obscure metaphysical concepts.<br /> <br /> <br /> I feel we need some Kung Fu Numina, I'm working on it. The problem is a lot of the character build concepts would use things like Merits, but how CWOD merits work they are undesirable compared to NWOD/Exalted Merits.<br /> <br /> <br /> I want a Book Dedicated to Extraordinary Citizens and Enlightened Science in the hands of nonMages. And some Supernatural Martials Arts love.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not wrong, but the Polynesian version is the one that's the source of the usage in video and tabletop games, not the Latin derived one.<br /> <br /> As for Kung Fu Numina, there's Demon Hunter X which does it quite well.<br /> <br /> I'd love to have the Extraordinary Citizen's Field Guide and Sorcerer's Handbook though. You could probably make an entire 300+ page book covering the various types of magical powers like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}